# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repo is a workspace: other repositories are cloned alongside it and
# worked on concurrently. None of them belong in this repo's history.
#
# The root is therefore an allowlist, everything is ignored unless named
# below. A repo cloned into the root is ignored the moment it appears, with no
# .gitignore edit and nothing to remember. `make lint` fails if a nested repo
# is ever tracked anyway, so the two mechanisms cover each other.
#
# Adding a new tracked file at the root means adding it here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
!/.devcontainer/
!/.github/
!/.vscode/
!/docs/
!/.gitignore
!/.pymarkdown.json
!/CLAUDE.md
!/Makefile
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/shell.env.example
!/devcontainer-environment-variables.json.example
!/pyproject.toml
!/tests/
# Tracked so plugin tasks can `git add` a module under .claude/plugins/ with
# no -f flag needed. .claude/settings.local.json stays ignored: its own
# later, more specific entry below still wins over this broader re-include.
!/.claude/
# The agent-agnostic canonical skills home (.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md,
# every name gd-*-prefixed). The plugin's skills/ entry at
# .claude/plugins/devcontainer/skills is a relative symlink into it, not a
# copy, so exactly one copy of every skill body exists.
!/.agents/
# The Terraform module (provider/aws) and the shared Terragrunt layer under
# remote-instances/ (its README, root.hcl and _envcommon/) (E5, spec
# Sections 5.6, 5.7) are tracked, while a per-instance deployment scaffold
# is not: `make instance-init` appends remote-instances/<name>/ to this
# file, keeping every scaffold local to its checkout until the developer
# promotes it deliberately by deleting that appended line. Both re-includes
# are directory-only; see tests/gitignore_check.py for why a `git
# check-ignore` query for either needs the directory form only while
# nothing exists at that path for git to stat.
!/provider/
!/remote-instances/
# The folder is tracked so it exists in a fresh clone; what you clone into
# it is not. VS Code still finds those repositories, because its scan walks
# directories rather than consulting .gitignore.
!/repos/
/repos/*
!/repos/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-developer identity and secrets. The .example files above are committed;
# these are generated from them and reach the remote container only through
# Parameter Store. Listed explicitly so they stay ignored even if the
# allowlist above is edited.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/shell.env
/devcontainer-environment-variables.json
.devcontainer/aws-profile-map.json
.devcontainer/hostcreds.map.json
.devcontainer/devcontainer-lock.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Environment files
shell.env
devcontainer-environment-variables.json

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/

# Terraform / Terragrunt working directories. `terraform init` downloads
# provider binaries here -- hundreds of megabytes of them -- and nothing in
# this cache belongs in version control. Without this rule a routine
# `terraform init` followed by `git add -A` stages those binaries, and the
# only thing that catches it is the secret scanner refusing to decode them.
.terraform/

# Terragrunt download and module caches under per-instance directories.
remote-instances/*/.terragrunt-cache/

# Per-instance scaffolds are local-only; promote deliberately by moving the directory into tracked scope.
remote-instances/*/.terraform.lock.hcl

# Host-side uv project environments must never live in this bind-mounted
# workspace (see Makefile UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT); ignored in case a bare
# `uv run` creates one anyway.
.venv/
